.env
**/.env
# Every dotenv sibling, not just `.env` itself. A dev machine can hold any
# number of them (`.env.local`, an `.env.portless` an older haven left behind),
# and a copy inside the build context would bake a dev stack's values —
# retention default, admin password, access tokens — into the image and let them
# win over whatever the deployment configured.
.env.*
**/.env.*
# `.env.example` is tracked documentation with no secrets in it.
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
**/.venv

